  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to compute the aspiration level (mean of outcomes ignoring probabilities), identify the positive differences from that level, and then compare the probability of those positive differences. The verbal report does not mention the aspiration level, nor does it refer to differences between outcomes and a mean. Instead, the individual compares the absolute monetary difference (100 Euros) and the small difference in probability (1%), and chooses the higher potential gain. This indicates that the individual did not use the aspiration-level-based rule. The information considered (monetary gain and probability difference) differs from the required elements of the decision reason. The justification is inconsistent with the rule of preferring the lottery with the higher probability of positive differences from the aspiration level. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The assessment is 0.",
